<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef generally steady on mostly moderate demand and offerings. Select rib, round and loin cuts steady to firm, while chuck cuts weak. Choice chuck, round and loin cuts generally steady, while rib cuts mostly firm.</p>
<p>Beef trimmings generally steady on light demand and offerings.-USDA</p>
<p>264 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p> 10 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>54 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     105.77	105.33	100.31	 99.65</p>
<p>Changes	  0.31	  0.20	  0.13	  0.16</p>
<p>Rib	  158.97	159.75	149.02	149.64</p>
<p>Chuck	 74.23	 70.84	 73.98	 71.00</p>
<p>Round	 90.97	 90.97	 87.24	 87.24</p>
<p>Loin	 168.21	170.46	151.59	152.36</p>
<p>Brisket     59.91	 59.91	 60.44	 60.44</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  71.12	 71.02	 71.39	 71.19</p>
<p>Flank	 60.86	 60.86	 61.09	 61.09</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
